        {
          "gap": "Direct 2022 evidence on expert appointments and institutional risk reduction inside the nuclear/security apparatus is sparse.",
          "lenses": ["1B.7", "1B.9"],
          "best_source_or_query_direction": "Russian-language reporting, Kremlin personnel decrees, and contemporaneous analysis of nuclear/security leadership changes in 2022.",
          "why_it_matters": "This is the main missing discriminator for whether Putin strengthened safety expertise or merely escalated rhetorically."
        }
      ],
      "reason": "The package fairly shows dangerous nuclear rhetoric, treaty obstruction, and Zaporizhzhia-related risk, but some of the supporting material is external reaction or retrospective context. It needs a tighter official 2022 record on doctrine, safety, and appointments before it is fully robust."
